title HUNK17 — the Skate view of a cursor's neighbors (cursor_preview.rye)
prompt Autonomous recursion lap: continue the Season-A Photos journey Lindy-first crux-first after HUNK16 sent; land a clean self-contained increment, send it as its own signed round, stop at custody gates.
think After HUNK16 (the edit cursor) the design doc named a Skate-painted cursor door. Chose the redo preview: symmetric to HUNK15's revert preview but driven by the cursor, and it carries the one property only a cursor can offer — a rewound cursor RETAINS its redo tail, so preview_redo shows a real image of the road ahead, where a plain revert (having thrown its tail away) cannot. That makes it the crux tie-in to HUNK16, not a redundant re-do of HUNK15.
think brushstroke/cursor_preview.rye: preview_at walks a VALUE COPY of the cursor to a clamped position and hands its applied prefix to HUNK13's edit_preview.preview — the caller's cursor untouched (EditCursor is a fixed array plus a u32, so the copy is independent). preview_undo/preview_redo are the one-step neighbors. Pure composition over two proven seams (HUNK16 cursor + HUNK13 preview), no new failure mode.
think Only a symlink was needed — edit_cursor.rye into brushstroke/, beside the qoi/photos/photo_edits/photo_revert/skate_grid/image_skate links already there.
obs Proofs over the HUNK13/HUNK15 8x8 two-tone (flip_h swaps red/blue): a two-flip history rewound one step previews its undo to the original (left cell red), its redo to the retained tail cell-for-cell, the current view differing (left cell blue); three previews leave the cursor exactly where it stood (untouched). The crux tie-in: a fresh push at the rewound position forgets the tail, so preview_redo falls back to the current view — proven equal cell-for-cell AND equal to a direct apply of flip_h then crop, so the new road is genuinely the pushed verbs.
obs Reds/ratchet caught: tame_style_check flagged four compound asserts in cursor_preview.rye and, on inspection, HUNK16's image/edit_cursor.rye carried eight of the same — they had slipped because the tame scan fixture does not cover image/. Split all twelve (each half named) as an additive tidy in this round; both witnesses re-run GREEN, TAME bans now clean, width exit 0.
obs No custody gate reached — a pure look over the edit-list; no name, no bead, no key, no funds, no network. HUNK16 and HUNK13 witnesses GREEN beneath.
loom witness=hunk_cursor_preview_witness image=8x8 grid=2x2 lit=256 result=GREEN
file brushstroke/cursor_preview.rye HUNK17 — preview_at/preview_undo/preview_redo over a cursor's neighbors; a value copy walks, the cursor untouched; selftest GREEN.
